abstract: >-
  Mergen-21 is a fully open-source 21 cm hydrogen line radio telescope
  built as a graduation project at Özyeğin University. The system consists
  of a laser-cut pyramidal horn antenna (16.9 dBi, 1420.405 MHz), a
  cascaded RF receiver chain (about 39.5 dB gain +/- 0.5 dB, about 1.5 dB
  noise figure), and a GNU Radio / ADALM-PLUTO SDR backend. First-light
  galactic-plane observations, showing pointing-dependent hydrogen-line
  detections, were recorded in April 2026 from Istanbul, Turkey. A
  Galactic rotation curve via the tangent-point method is a future goal
  and is not part of the released results. All hardware design files,
  simulation data, measurement data, and analysis software are published
  under open licenses.
